        "name": "emit-activity-fact-on-article",
        "description": "WS-A PRODUCER wiring (2nd source) — proves the feed is GENERATIVE: a totally different source is ONE DATA row, zero handler code change (deletion/emergence test made concrete). On a content-generation.article-result write (an AI worker published an article), dispatch action:activity-feed.emit-activity-fact with its OWN actor_type/action_type (publish, not write). Only possible because emit-activity-fact was made input-bound (a3e8a6ea); a hardcoded actor_type='ai-agent'/action_type='write' handler would have mislabeled this source. Pure DATA over trigger-engine -> slot::workflow (L136). Arms after the next fold/boot.",
        "is_active": true,
        "version": 0,
        "trigger_type": "delta",
        "match_condition": {
          "conditions": [
